WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.570
Every startup deck tells a story. VCR2 checks
whether the numbers behind it really reconcile.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.790
Founders send a deck, a model and an update, with
every headline number computed by the company itself.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.540
VCR2 rebuilds those numbers from the company's
own data, in minutes instead of days.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.430
Take this sample company.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.960
Its deck claims 134% net revenue retention.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.470
Rebuilt from its customer ledger, it's 98.8%.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.240
35 points in the company's favour,
and a question for the founders.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.590
Built for investors, it's free, and
nothing you enter leaves your browser.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.550
It rebuilds revenue, tests the billing,
and models the runway and the deal.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.560
Let's open the Series A example.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.090
Its customer ledger and monthly financials
come straight from Excel or CSV,

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.130
parsed locally, with no AI required.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.650
Then you work through ten short evidence
sections, with live figures updating as you type.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.010
Every value is tagged with its
source, so you know what's verified.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.480
Before any score, VCR2 reconciles everything:
here, nine material contradictions.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.870
Revenue, retention and growth are all overstated,
and ten of twelve gaps favour the company.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.870
Every metric is recomputed from raw figures.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.600
The score is withheld until the gaps are resolved.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.340
No false confidence: every number
on the report is explained.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:49.230
Forensic tests scan the billing data: a final-month spike,
one-off customers counted as recurring, possible duplicates.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.580
Each one shows its method and its limits.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:59.090
Four thousand simulated paths give the odds of reaching
the next round before cash runs out: just two percent.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.740
The deal maths is done for you: post-money,
dilution, and the exit it takes to return the fund.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.980
Down to the full liquidation waterfall.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.330
Every gap becomes a question for the founders,
ranked by what would change the decision.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.200
Ready to send as an email.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.850
One click prints the investment committee memo.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.860
Your library benchmarks each
deal against your own portfolio,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.310
and the owner Studio tunes the engine, with no code.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:37.290
VCR2. Evidence first. Fully explained. Completely private.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.060
Try it free at vcr2.app.
